    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Project description'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/OPSScoring/Projectdescription?rev=' id='Projectdescription' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/OPSScoring' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1440' minheight='1000' minwidth='1440' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='7000' id='3' name='OPS Scoring description' w='98888' x='556' y='800'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='91400' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98888' x='556' y='7800'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The OPS Scoring project aims to </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>evaluate the quality of our operations</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> within DH Kitchens compared to the B&amp;M branches of live kitchen brands.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>This project benchmarks kitchen vendors against brick-and-mortar vendors using the following </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>six key OPS metrics</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Preparation Time</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Rating</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Vendor late 5 min</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Rejection Rate</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Offline Time</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- At vendor time</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Scores</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> can </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>range from 1 to 5</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, with 1 indicating poor performance and 5 indicating excellent performance.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Individual metrics are first scored. For instance, consider Preparation Time, where we compare our vendors&apos; performance to their B&amp;M branches using </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>the average for the last four weeks</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 1</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was significantly slower than B&amp;M branches (statistical test confirms significance).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 2</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was slower than B&amp;M branches, but the difference was not statistically significant.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 3</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Performance was the same as B&amp;M branches.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 4</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was quicker than B&amp;M branches, but the difference was not statistically significant.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 5</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was significantly quicker than B&amp;M branches (statistical test confirms significance).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The individual results for each of the six metrics are summed to calculate an average, referred to as the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>OPS score</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> in the dashboard. Currently, </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>all metrics are equally weighted</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, with no special weighting applied to any specific KPI.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>To increase the accuracy and reliability of our OPS scoring, we compare metrics based on the last four weeks instead of a single week. This provides a larger dataset, allowing us to better assess significance and ensure that less frequent metrics, such as Ratings, are more consistently included in the scoring.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Kruskal-Wallis test</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, a statistical tool, was employed to evaluate significance. This test is particularly useful for determining significant differences between group averages, especially with non-normally distributed data. Its applicability to &quot;skewed&quot; data, common in business scenarios where values cluster at one end, makes it highly beneficial. The Kruskal-Wallis test enables confident group comparisons and data-driven decisions, even when data patterns are not symmetrical.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='15' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='14' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone fixed-size='62' h='7000' id='3' is-fixed='true' name='OPS Scoring description' w='98888' x='556' y='800'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='91400' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98888' x='556' y='7800'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The OPS Scoring project aims to </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>evaluate the quality of our operations</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> within DH Kitchens compared to the B&amp;M branches of live kitchen brands.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>This project benchmarks kitchen vendors against brick-and-mortar vendors using the following </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>six key OPS metrics</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Preparation Time</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Rating</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Vendor late 5 min</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Rejection Rate</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Offline Time</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- At vendor time</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Scores</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> can </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>range from 1 to 5</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, with 1 indicating poor performance and 5 indicating excellent performance.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Individual metrics are first scored. For instance, consider Preparation Time, where we compare our vendors&apos; performance to their B&amp;M branches using </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>the average for the last four weeks</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 1</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was significantly slower than B&amp;M branches (statistical test confirms significance).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 2</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was slower than B&amp;M branches, but the difference was not statistically significant.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 3</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Performance was the same as B&amp;M branches.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 4</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was quicker than B&amp;M branches, but the difference was not statistically significant.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>- Score 5</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>: Vendor was significantly quicker than B&amp;M branches (statistical test confirms significance).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The individual results for each of the six metrics are summed to calculate an average, referred to as the </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>OPS score</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'> in the dashboard. Currently, </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>all metrics are equally weighted</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, with no special weighting applied to any specific KPI.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>To increase the accuracy and reliability of our OPS scoring, we compare metrics based on the last four weeks instead of a single week. This provides a larger dataset, allowing us to better assess significance and ensure that less frequent metrics, such as Ratings, are more consistently included in the scoring.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>The </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Kruskal-Wallis test</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>, a statistical tool, was employed to evaluate significance. This test is particularly useful for determining significant differences between group averages, especially with non-normally distributed data. Its applicability to &quot;skewed&quot; data, common in business scenarios where values cluster at one end, makes it highly beneficial. The Kruskal-Wallis test enables confident group comparisons and data-driven decisions, even when data patterns are not symmetrical.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{9230865A-6E5F-40E9-A976-541AD9C21FEA}' />
    </dashboard>
